# Issue Priority Title Policy

## Purpose

When the current open GitHub issues in one repository are re-ranked, encode
that unique order only in issue titles as `P<n> <remainder>`. `P1` is the
highest priority. `n` equals the number of currently open issues. This rule
does not assign MoSCoW classes and does not authorize other issue workflows
to invent P-number prefixes.

## Apply when

Use this rule while listing open issues, ranking them, confirming a ranked
title set, or applying those titles. Other issue create, refine, or update
workflows MUST NOT add, compact, or rewrite `P<n>` prefixes unless they are
executing this dedicated reprioritization workflow.

## Required numbering

MUST:

- Rank only currently open GitHub issues. Exclude pull requests. Leave closed
  issues unchanged.
- Assign unique consecutive integers from 1 through n, with n equal to the
  current open-issue count. Do not share a number and do not leave gaps.
- Use the exact title form `P<n> <remainder>`.
- Strip a leading `P<digits>`, `P<digits>:`, or `[P<digits>]` prefix before
  composing the remainder. Preserve the remainder text. Do not invent a new
  title.
- Re-number the entire current open set on each authorized run. Closing an
  issue does not compact remaining numbers until this workflow runs again.

## Authorization and identity

MUST:

- Treat Command or Agent invocation as orchestration only.
- Wait for explicit user approval of the exact current issue-number set,
  order, and proposed titles, or a matching target-repository `AGENTS.md`
  policy that names that same repository, operation, and set.
- Re-read the live open-issue numbers immediately before any title write.
  Stop when the live set does not match the approved set.
- Change only the title through `update-github-issue`. Do not change body,
  labels, assignees, milestone, or state.
- Continue remaining title writes after a partial failure. Do not roll back
  successful title writes.

MUST NOT:

- Treat a recommended order as a confirmed ranking.
- Guess ranks for issues that appeared after the approved inventory.
- Convert a truncated list into a complete ranking.
- Use `prioritize-product-issues` or parent-issue MoSCoW ranking as the
  title-prefix source of truth.

## Examples

Positive: Ten currently open issues become `P1` through `P10` after the user
confirms that exact ordered title list, then each title is patched or left as
`no_op` when it already matches.

Negative: Creating a new issue with an invented `P3` prefix, or giving two
open issues `P1`, violates this rule.
